    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2TFKvRBg92qB2mTn4oNeRpi)_\n\nBefore: `emacsclient -c` against the daemon opens a frame that disappears almost immediately.\n\nAfter: the client frame stays open and is centered on screen.\n\n`sp-frame.el` adds `sp-frame-recenter` to `after-make-frame-functions` but nothing defines it. The function got lost when `lem-frame-recenter` from lambda-emacs was renamed to the `sp-` prefix. Every frame made through `make-frame` (which is every `emacsclient -c` frame) signals a void-function error. The server then returns the error to the client and deletes the frame it just created. A plain GUI launch never hits this because its initial frame doesn't run that hook.\n\nHow: restore the function under its `sp-` name, with the same body as `lem-frame-recenter` in `lambda-emacs-modified/.../lem-setup-frames.el`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01G1V2dppJWyRgELZAAtdqE5)_",
